      "text": "shall break one of these least commandments, Matt. 5:19. thieves break through and steal, Matt. 6:19. brake, and gave the loaves, Matt. 14:19 (Mark 6:41; Luke 9:16). they took up of the broken meat, Matt. 15:37. fall on this stone shall be broken, Matt. 21:44 (Luke 20:18). suffered his house to be broken up, Matt. 24:43. she brake the box, and poured it on his head, Mark 14:3. multitude of fishes: and their net brake, Luke 5:6. he not only had broken the sabbath, John 5:18. the scripture cannot be broken, John 10:35. besought Pilate that their legs might be broken, John 19:31. disciples came together to break bread, Acts 20:7. What mean ye to weep and to break mine heart, Acts 21:13. because of unbelief they were broken off, Rom. 11:20. this is my body, which is broken for you, 1 Cor. 11:24. hath broken down the middle wall of partition, Eph. 2:14.",
